{
	"version": 5,
	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "eHmFySvoafAoJAKce",
			"description": "Hand Flamer",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A compact, one-handed flame weapon carried by Adepta Sororitas Seraphim and Inquisitorial agents for close-quarters purging; background stresses its short reach compared with a full flamer, traded for one-handed use alongside a second weapon or wargear item.\n\nDesign: Built bottom-up rather than from an anchor, since the framework's weapon table has none for flame weapons: base damage and cone length scale down from the standard Flamer entry below in the same rough proportion the bolt and plasma families use for their pistol-scale members (2d+2 burn and a 3-yard cone versus the Flamer's 4d and 5 yards). Checked by exact dice distribution: average roll 9 penetrates flak (now DR 30, up from DR 12 across two rounds of the armour rescale) on essentially 0% of hits — a flamer was never an armour-piercing weapon and the cone attack now cannot scratch even flak at all, so the real threat is entirely the DR-ignoring follow-up below; this is an honest consequence of the armour rescale landing on a family whose raw cone damage was never itself anchored high, not a departure from the flame family's original design intent. The clinging, DR-ignoring follow-up and the cover-bypassing behaviour are the two lore properties the assignment calls out for the whole flame family; both are given the same treatment as the Flamer entry so they read identically across every weapon in this file. The follow-up's sealed-armour exemption is a deliberate new rule for this Rescale: without it, a weapon whose whole selling point is bypassing armour would trivialise Astartes power armour turn after turn, which the fiction never shows — flame weapons are feared by infantry in flak, mesh or carapace, and by anyone whose suit isn't sealed, but a battle-brother who keeps his helmet locked shrugs off the fire itself. Handling: weight (5 lb), min ST (8), Bulk (-2) and Shots 3(5) are unchanged; this is a one-handed weapon and RoF/Rcl/Acc don't apply to a cone attack (B412), so there is no RoF figure to correct here the way there is for the ranged weapons elsewhere in this project.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adepta Sororitas",
				"Inquisition"
			],
