				},
				{
					"id": "W7t-lVcknaLiUpiZf",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "burn",
						"base": "1d-1"
					},
					"range": "3",
					"shots": "3(5)",
					"bulk": "-2",
					"strength": "8",
					"usage": "Follow-up (per turn while ablaze)",
					"usage_notes": "A target who fails an HT roll on being hit catches fire and takes this every turn until extinguished (see B433's fire rules); this damage is not stopped by DR, since it is the promethium burning on and around the target rather than a fresh attack. This assumes exposed flesh, cloth or open-visored armour the fire can actually catch on: against a hermetically sealed suit (Astartes or Terminator power armour with the helmet locked, a void suit, etc.) the follow-up does not apply at all unless the seal has already been breached that scene (GM's call) — promethium can wash across ceramite for a turn or two of cosmetic flame, but it has nothing to ignite.\n",
