		{
			"id": "ebfiQV8_LdKNGCFmC",
			"description": "Heavy Flamer",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A heavier, hotter-burning flame weapon mounted on vehicles or carried by Astartes Devastator/ Aggressor-adjacent squads and Inquisitorial storm troopers; background treats it as a bunker- and horde-clearing weapon with a longer, wider cone and a bigger promethium reservoir than a standard flamer.\n\nDesign: One die over the standard Flamer's new 4d (so 5d burn), with a longer 8-yard cone and a bigger fuel tank (6 bursts vs 4), on a much higher ST 12 reflecting a genuinely heavy weapon usually carried by an Astartes or mounted on a vehicle sponson. Average roll 17.5 penetrates flak (now DR 30, up from the DR 12 this entry was first checked against) on 0% of hits and still fails against carapace (DR 70: 0%), by exact dice distribution — the heavy flamer's raw cone hit no longer beats flak either, after two rounds of the armour rescale; it remains a decisive threat only to unarmoured infantry, and its actual bunker-clearing reputation now rests entirely on the DR-ignoring burning follow-up, more so than when this entry was first written. The DR-ignoring burning follow-up is scaled the same amount as the base damage and carries the same sealed-armour exemption as the Hand Flamer and Flamer above, keeping the same design relationship used across the family.",
