		{
			"id": "e4RaY3j6tlDjrPm4W",
			"description": "Promethium Fuel Canister",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The sealed, pressurised fuel reservoir every flame weapon in this file draws from; background material treats spare canisters as standard squad-level resupply, carried by an ammo-bearer or strapped to the weapon itself, and as a minor hazard in their own right if struck by enemy fire.\n\nDesign: A plain reload item rather than a weapon: swapping one in restores a flame weapon's shots to its listed maximum (the number after the slash in each weapon's shots field above). No separate stat block is needed since the fuel itself has no damage value; a GM wanting a \"canister explodes if shot\" hazard can rule it detonates for the carrying weapon's own cone damage.",
